Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.27,0:00:01.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}So, two questions.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.34,0:00:03.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}When will it flip next?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.07,0:00:05.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}And {\c&H00A1ED&}how often{\c&HF7F4F2&} does it flip?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.37,0:00:07.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Which one can we answer?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.23,0:00:14.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}In a simple computer model of a\Nflipping {\c&H3468EB&}field{\c&HF7F4F2&}, the first is hopeless.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.96,0:00:16.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}The second is not.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.32,0:00:20.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Finding out why takes us\Nthrough liquid metal and chaos.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.13,0:00:25.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Then to {\c&HF09CB4&}machines{\c&HF7F4F2&} that dream up\Nsnapshots of magnetic fields.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.60,0:00:30.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}They must obey some laws exactly,\Nand others only on average.
